      "rationale": "The ledger clip explicitly states the HA tag was introduced at amino acid position 234 of full-length human TASK-4 (KCNK17) and detected by a chemiluminescence surface assay, confirming extracellular accessibility. Python verification confirms position 234 (S) lies within the second extracellular loop (topology landmarks: EC2 = 201-243), 34 residues from the upstream TM2 boundary (200) and 10 residues from the downstream TM3 boundary (244), both well above the >=3 residue minimum. No cysteines or N-glycosylation sequons (NxS/T) are present in EC2, and no disulfide or active-site constraints are flagged. The junction is taken as insert_after=234 (tag between S234 and Q235), the most natural reading of 'introduced at amino acid position 234'; the one-residue ambiguity (233 vs 234) does not affect extracellular placement. Full-length human TASK-4 (KCNK17) expressed in HEK293 or similar cells; a 9-aa HA tag (YPYDVPDYA) was introduced at amino acid position 234, placing it in the second extracellular loop (EC2, residues 201-243). The construct was used in a chemiluminescence surface-expression assay.",
